<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" modified="2026-06-11T00:00:00.000Z" agent="Trae"><diagram id="pipeline" name="Pipeline"><mxGraphModel dx="1800" dy="2600" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2200" pageHeight="3200" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="header" value="SciAtlas Idea Generation Pipeline&#10;Run dir: /REDACTED/tiaozhanbei/chemstry_question/07-&#10;AI与化学未来/full&#10;Topic: Research question: Will AI redefine the future of&#10;chemistry?&#10;Context: AI and machine learning have the potential to&#10;greatly benefit organic chemistry, leading to more rapid&#10;synthesis of molecules. These computational technologies&#10;can greatly optimize and accelerate drug development by,&#10;for example, predicting successful pathways to synthesize&#10;target molecules.&#10;Status: ok&#10;Failed step: N/A" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="40" y="40" width="435" height="258" /></mxCell><mxCell id="params" value="Input Parameters&#10;topic: Research question: Will AI redefine the future of&#10;chemistry?&#10;Context: AI and machine learning have the potential to&#10;greatly benefit organic chemistry, leading to more rapid&#10;synthesis of molecules. These computational technologies&#10;can greatly optimize and accelerate drug development by,&#10;for example, predicting successful pathways to synthesize&#10;target molecules.&#10;domain: Chemistry&#10;workflow_mode: full&#10;&#10;Effective Pipeline Config&#10;workflow_mode: full&#10;anchor_top_k: 5&#10;keyword_min_papers: 2&#10;k_step1: 4&#10;seed_num_queries: 8&#10;seed_per_query: 3&#10;seed_request_multiplier: 6&#10;seed_request_floor: 12&#10;seed_recent_years: 7&#10;seed_min_citations: 1000&#10;graph_budget_ratio: 0.35&#10;graph_budget_min: 12&#10;graph_budget_max: 30&#10;graph_max_predecessor