sion processes', 'Stochastic optimal control /&#10;model predictive control under uncertainty', 'Constraint-aware&#10;safe data-driven design for multi-step dynamical systems',&#10;'System identification from limited, noisy, biased data',&#10;'Explicit trade-off analysis between mechanistic recursion and&#10;direct endpoint prediction']&#10;combination_plan: Cast multi-step synthesis planning as a&#10;constrained stochastic predictive-control problem where&#10;reaction steps evolve a latent mechanistic state, and compare&#10;or hybridize mechanism-constrained recursive state-space&#10;models with direct multi-step predictors of route&#10;feasibility,...&#10;justification: The candidate paper provides a structural&#10;analogy between sequential control systems and multi-step&#10;synthesis planning: both require safe, uncertainty-aware,&#10;multi-horizon prediction under constraints. Its contrast&#10;between recursive state-space modeling and direct multi-step&#10;p...&#10;abstract: This paper contrasts recursive state space models&#10;and direct multi-step predictors for linear predictive&#10;control. We provide a tutorial exposition for both model&#10;structures to solve the following problems: 1. stochastic&#10;optimal control; 2. system identification; 3. stochastic..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#ead1dc;strokeColor=#a64d79;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="11614" width="620" height="1770" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step8_selected_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step8_selected_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step9" value="Step 9 Idea Generation&#10;status: completed&#10;idea_count: 1&#10;round: 3" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="60" y="13484" width="220" height="96" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step_step8_step_step9" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step_step9"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step9_ideas_panel" value="Step 9 Idea Generation + Novelty Check&#10;count: 1&#10;&#10;1. Causal Mechanism-State Model Predictive Planning for&#10;Repairable Retrosynthesis&#10;novelty_level: medium&#10;motivation: AI can redefine chemistry only if planning systems&#10;move from isolated step prediction to robust, repairable multi-&#10;step synthesis. Template-free graph-to-sequence models showed&#10;that retrosynthesis and reaction prediction can be learned end-&#10;to-end [Author et al., 2021](https://openalex.org/W3206796875).&#10;Mechanism-aware bond-change models improve data efficiency and&#10;chemical plausibility for reaction outcomes [Author...&#10;methods: 1. Causal mechanism-state representation with formal&#10;belief revision: Represent each route as a trajectory of&#10;mechanistic state vectors s_t over molecular graphs, protecting-&#10;group occupancy, chemoselectivity masks, catalyst-condition&#10;compatibility, poison or impurity accumulation, and calibrated&#10;outcome beliefs. Repair actions are explicit causal&#10;interventions do(a), including reaction step, protecting-group&#10;change, catalyst substitution, purification, workup, or&#10;condition adjustment. A projection operator updat...&#10;novelty_justification: The closest existing combination is&#10;MechRetro together with the cited step-level predictors:&#10;template-free retrosynthesis/reaction prediction, chemistry-&#10;aware Diels-Alder outcome modeling, and meta-learning&#10;selectivity prediction. MechRetro already supplies mechanism-&#10;aware, interpretable retrosynthetic pathway planning, while the&#10;other references supply plausible frozen predictors for&#10;individual reaction outcomes....&#10;improvement_suggestions: ['Sharpen the mechanistic novelty by&#10;defining a formal structural causal model for synthesis routes&#10;in which each do(a) repair action is a mechanism-preserving&#10;graph rewrite, such as electron-flow transformation, protecting-&#10;group lability, catalyst poisoning, or impurity removal, and&#10;derive identifiable counterfactual repair estimands or bounds&#10;from that model.', 'Replace or constrain the generic learned&#10;transition function with an invariant-conserving mechanistic&#10;operator that explicitly propagates atom/electron balance,&#10;protecting-group occupancy, catalyst-poison load, and&#10;chemoselectivity masks, then show that these conservation laws&#10;are necessary for repair success rather than merely auxiliary&#10;features.', 'Make the learned incompatibility graph&#10;scientifically central by proving or testing that recovery of&#10;intervention-specific mechanistic edges, such as catalyst poison&#10;causing downstream selectivity loss, is necessary for successful&#10;route repair and cannot be obtained from correlational route&#10;features alone.']" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="13484" width="680" height="960" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step9_ideas_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step9" target="step9_ideas_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="retrieval_1" value="Retrieval 1&#10;step: step1&#10;command: search-papers&#10;cache_hit: False&#10;paper_count: 18&#10;&#10;Parameters&#10;query_text: reinforcement learning and multi-objective&#10;optimization of synthesizable drug candidates&#10;keywords: [{'text': 'reinforcement learning', 'score':&#10;10}, {'text': 'learning multi', 'score': 9}, {'text':&#10;'multi objective', 'score': 8}, {'text': 'objective&#10;optimization', 'score': 7}, {'text': 'optimization&#10;synthesizable', 'score': 6}]&#10;source_type: idea_text&#10;top_k: 18&#10;retrieval_mode: hybrid&#10;target_field: Chemistry&#10;&#10;Returned Papers&#10;1. Bayesian Optimization over Multiple Experimental&#10;Fidelities Accelerates Automated Discovery of Drug&#10;Molecules (2025) [score=0.5822]&#10;Abstract: Different experiments of differing fidelities&#10;are commonly used in the search for new drug molecules. In&#10;classic experimental funnels, libraries of molecules&#10;undergo sequential rounds of virtual, coarse, and refined&#10;experimental screenings, with each level balanced between&#10;the...&#10;&#10;2. An exploration strategy improves the diversity of de&#10;novo ligands using deep reinforcement learning: a case for&#10;the adenosine A2A receptor (2019) [score=0.5576]&#10;Abstract: N/A&#10;&#10;3. Multiobjective de novo drug design with recurrent&#10;neural networks and nondominated sorting (2020)&#10;[score=0.5359]&#10;Abstract: N/A&#10;&#10;4. DeepGraphMol, a multi-objective, computational strategy&#10;for generating molecules with desirable properties: a&#10;graph convolution and reinforcement learning approach&#10;(2020) [score=0.5179]&#10;Abstract: Abstract We address the problem of generating&#10;novel molecules with desired interaction properties as a&#10;multi-objective optimization problem. Interaction binding&#10;models are learned from binding data using graph&#10;convolution networks (GCNs). Since the experimentally&#10;obtained prop...&#10;&#10;5. Multi-Objective Optimization Methods in De Novo Drug&#10;Design (2012) [score=0.5053]&#10;Abstract: De-novo drug design (DND) is a complex&#10;procedure, requiring the satisfaction of many&#10;pharmaceutically important objectives. Several&#10;computational methodologies employing various optimization&#10;approaches have been developed to search for